### Grid System & Movement Logic
```
Grid Dimensions: 5 rows × 11 columns = 55 aliens maximum
Initial Position: x ∈ [-4.5, 4.5], y = 2.0 to -2.0 (world space)
Movement Vector: v = (dx, 0), dx cycles between +0.3 and -0.3 units/frame

Edge Detection Algorithm:
  For each alien in current row:
    if alien.x + alien.width/2 > rightBoundary → reverse direction
    if alien.x - alien.width/2 < leftBoundary → reverse direction
  All aliens move as single unit (synchronized)

Descent Mechanic:
  Upon edge hit: y -= 0.3, flip dx sign
  Descent speed increases exponentially with each row cleared
```

